  "resolved_review_findings": [
    {
      "finding": "Original commit-tree parser skipped non-blob Git entries, allowing a gitlink delta to escape exact migration path closure.",
      "resolution": "Parser now rejects unsupported entries; the latest focused receipt includes a real clean committed 160000-entry rejection test."
    }
  ],
  "source_review": [
    "Ordinary tracked payloads retain exact raw Git-blob equality; unselected literal pointer text remains ordinary.",
    "Canonical v1 three-field pointers bind a lowercase SHA-256 OID and canonical bounded size. Pointer Git identity and hydrated payload raw-Git/SHA256 identities remain separate.",
    "The identified commit or stage-zero index supplies attribute authority. A private repository excludes source info/attributes, caller Git overrides and global/system attributes.",
    "Isolated validation verifies hydration, creates an owned private object cache, uses known local skip-download filters and disables hooks. It copies no source remotes or credential configuration.",
    "The no-rewrite planner verifies exact original payloads; migration verification requires original ancestry, complete archive/path closure, exact attributes/pointers and unchanged payloads.",
    "The dedicated Git/LFS tests remain outside default core discovery; zero-object bootstrap validation does not require an LFS executable.",
    "Existing workflows only gain checkout hydration; their manual/default-false execution policy remains byte-identical otherwise."
  ],
